ef  history of One Piece now I don't know if  you've ever tried to convince someone to  take the plunge and start reading the  series but it can be quite of a hard  sell watching a 26 episode series can be  enough of a commitment by itself but  asking someone to read or watch 1 000  chapters slash episodes it can seem  downright daunting for very obvious  reasons not to mention that maybe some  people are turned off by the cartoonish  looking art style thinking it's not as  serious or cool as some of their other  favorite series well I'm here to change  your mind about that thanks to a uh  let's say questionable four kids dub and  a few other factors one piece has had a  hard time growing its fan base in the  west compared to a series like Dragon  Ball or Naruto but let's look at the  facts this is the most successful manga  of all time and one of the most  successful pieces of literature Ever One  Piece has outsold every other comic  series but Superman that means that its  sales numbers have beaten out both  Spider-Man and Batman whose publication  histories predate one piece by many many  decades and the estimated sales for the  series plays 80 to order its author  within the top 10 best-selling authors  of all time he's just past Dr Zeus and  soon one piece will even outsell a hairy  Potter simply put one piece with a  serialization spanning 25 years is a  worldwide sales Juggernaut why because  it's just that good before we get  started though you might want to know  some of the basics so what is one piece  about one piece takes place 20 years  after the execution of the notorious  King of the Pirates gold Roger on The  Executioner's stand Roger announced the  world that he left his treasure the one  piece hidden somewhere out in the  world's most danger accuracy the grand  line a terrifying strip of ocean that  spans Once Around the Globe the  announcement of this great treasure led  to a great age of piracy which brings us  to our protagonist Monkey D Luffy a  rambunctious young pirate who has rubber  Powers thanks to eating a devil fruit a  magical type of fruit that bestows  special abilities to someone who eats  them but at the same time also renders  them unable to swim a pretty big  drawback in a story that takes place on  the high seas and so throughout Luffy's  Adventure he gathers together a crew of  equally unique characters to fight side  by side as he takes on Rival Pirates and  the world government in an attempt to  fight the world's greatest treasure  overall there are really four great  qualities that make one piece Stand Out  Among its peers the World building the  plots the characters and the tone aren't  there any more qualities than these that  make one piece fantastic of course there  are but we don't want to get into any  dangerous spoiler territory in this  video and dampen your experience of the  series so without further Ado let's get  into chapter two the world of One Piece  if you ask the average fan what their  favorite thing about one piece is a lot  of them will say it's outstanding World  building if all you've ever seen is  promotional images it probably seems  like one piece is just a nice little  story where our crew sails around the  world getting into hijinks what I  definitely wasn't ready for when I  started the series was a complex web of  political Intrigue that easily stands on  the level of a series like Game of  Thrones or Lord of the Rings so if you  really enjoy fleshed out fantasy worlds  you will definitely fall in love with  the world of one piece this world is  filled with pirates searching for the  ultimate treasure the one piece but  along the way our crew visits a lot of  islands each with its own unique  governments culture creatures Etc and so  one Island may be filled with  prehistoric dinosaurs and battling  Giants whereas the next one is an  expansive desert Kingdom one Island may  be based on feudal Japan and another one  might be a dream Fields Candyland  straight out of a Disney movie and the  wildest thing about all of this is that  all these diverse places somehow form a  cohesive whole we don't simply stop off  somewhere and then Sail Away into the  Horizon never to think about these past  Islands ever again instead they all  interact seamlessly with one another and  the history of the world each kingdom or  Island the strawheads visit are  connected politically through the world  government a shadowy organization that  claims to uphold the peace and defend  the people from the evil Pirates but in  reality causes just as much or arguably  even more suffering as the Pirates do  the world of one piece is composed of  many different factions that move  independently from our main characters  and while the protagonist strawhead  Luffy certainly makes his mark on the  world he's just one small small fish in  a very big pond of characters while the  story sagas are shaped by the straw  Hat's actions the world is always moving  and shifting behind the scenes as well  between each major story arc ichiroda  shows us what the major players of the  world are up to elsewhere in no other  series will you see a fan base gets so  ecstatic about something as seemingly  simple as a newspaper but when big news  Morgans drops the latest issue you  better believe we're about to get some  mind-blowing updates about what's going  on without favorite characters simply  put this word doesn't seem just like a  game board for places to move on around  on it feels like a real living breathing  place and we care deeply about its many  inhabitants Oda has filled each and  every of these islands with so much care  and consideration that we're really on  the edge of our seats while we wait to  see how the complex political Dynamics  play out in the end and that is all  thanks to chapter three the character  and so of course we have to talk about  the stars of the show The Incredible web  of characters and wow does one piece  have some fantastic ones I mean with  over 1 000 characters in the series  there's a little something for everyone  here really but Central to one piece is  of course the straw hat crew our main  character Monkey D Luffy is unlike any  other Shonen protagonist just on the  surface level he seems to share some  essential traits with other Shonen  Heroes he's got the brains or black  thereof of Goku and a lofty goal like  Naruto but no one has the conviction  that Luffy does really and while he  really wouldn't do too well on his  standardized tests he has an intuitive  emotional intelligence that allows him  to make friends everywhere he goes more  than his rubber body his true power is  the way that he relates to others and  fights for those that he cares about  most of the time he's Carefree silly  even but when it's time to get serious  he'll send a a chill down your spine and  you'll be cheering for him when he gives  villains what they deserve which usually  is a really big punch the rest of the  crew is also fantastic the absolute  badass swordsman Zorro the greedy  Navigator Nami the Cowardly sniper who  saw piso way Chef Sanji the Cotton Candy  Loving reindeer Dr Chopper and a singing  skeleton named Brooke as well as some  others that I won't spoil for now  because their joining can come it's a  bit of a surprise I guess every one of  these characters not only has  spectacular Feats but they have dreams  and convictions that match their  Captain's dream to become the pirate's  King and while they're fun and even  silly on the surface they all have depth  as we learn about the tragedies they  suffered in their childhood that made  them who they are today we fall in love  with this cast of characters also you  will definitely 100 cry when you get to  some of their backstories so just be  ready for that of course our main crew  are only the beginning the straw hats  also encounter many many others on their  travels and some standouts are the  amazing villains the Marines are tasked  by the world governments to hunt down  the law-breaking Pirates which means  that our main cast constantly are on the  run from fearsome members like Captain  smoker or Admiral akind however there  are also of course opposing Pirates such  as the seven Warlords of the sea which  includes Fierce and intimidating  characters like the criminal mastermind  crocodile or the greatest swordsman in  the world's Dracula mihawk when we're  introduced to these characters they  appear as insurmountable obstacles some  of them are literally impossible to even  touch and so of course it makes it all  the more satisfying when Luffy and his  crew use their resolve and their skills  to overcome these villains and save the  innocent people on the islands they  encounter and speaking of those innocent  people the straw hats have their fair  share of allies on the sea is of the  ground line too some are royalty who  rule the various Islands they visit and  liberate such as nifatari Vivi the  princes of alabaster but some are even  fellow Pirates like the fan favorites  Trafalgar law and then of course there  are the legends who either in the past  or present have shaped the one piece  World itself people like gold Roger the  pirate who on the execution stance  started the great age of piracy by  telling people across the world to go  and search for his treasure the one  piece throughout the adventure of One  Piece you'll meet a fascinating cast of  people and if it sounds like a lot well  no worries there Oda takes his time in  each location and with each character to  let us get to know each of them as  people and to fully develop them  throughout the story it's one of the  many reasons that one piece's length  actually works in its favor it's all  killer no filler which brings me to  chapter four The Plot the plot of one  piece is another fantastic reason that  you you should read this series the  amazing thing about one piece isn't that  it has over 1 000 chapters it's that it  has 1 000 chapters and it's still going  strong the arcs being published right  now are some of the best one piece have  to offer and there's one simple reason  for this the mangaka Ichiro Ora planned  his story from the very beginning I know  that this seems trivial but you'd be  amazed at how many authors don't  actually know how their story will end  when they begin publication they just  kind of start from a premise and make it  up as they go along 25 years ago Luffy  set out to find the ultimate treasure  the one piece he's still searching for  that treasure and many are skeptical  that whatever it will be in the end will  be disappointing like the treasure will  be the friends you made along the way  however Oda Sensei has already gone on  record saying that the treasure is  something physical or at least part of  it he has had the final panel and the  overall story of the series planned for  decades and while he does insert fun  details and ideas along the way to  expand on the world that he's created  the broad Strokes of the story are  already well thought out I mean it would  have been one thing to have a great idea  for a pirate adventure and just letting  Luffy start his journey without having  the end in mind but eventually he  probably would have run out of ideas but  ever since the beginning Oda has been  constructing a story with One Singular  goal which honestly makes it such an  impressive series not just among manga  but among literature in general one way  that you can see this is with Ichiro  oda's masterful hints and foreshadowing  characters will be mentioned in the  early beginnings of the story only to  show up and play a very important role  hundreds of chapters later at points and  that really just goes to show the  thorough planning that went into  creating this masterfully structured  story not to take digs too hard at other  series but many of them seem to be  developed based on a central interesting  premise but eventually really start  falling apart the longer they get  because the storytellers didn't begin  with the ending in mind let's just call  it the JJ Abrams effect let's just leave  the world of anime for a second and  think about how TV shows like lost or  the much maligned Star Wars sequel  Trilogy Begin by Abram setting up so  many Mysteries so fans get sucked in by  all the Intrigue the problem is that  Abrams has not figured out what the  solution to the mystery really is and  seemingly also doesn't care leading to  his properties having terribly  disappointing endings many anime series  seem to suffer from the exact same  problem for instance in Bleach a series  that I really hold dear the soul Society  was a fantastic early Arc however it  does seem like titekubo the author  wasn't sure what should happen  afterwards so they just rinsed and  repeated with a new kidnapped Ally to  rescue and a new assortment of powerful  baddies to fight Dragon Ball Z kind of  does the same thing as well and two of  course can't forget the ending of Naruto  when we found out that big spoiler  Warning by the way skip ahead if you  don't want to hear this it was aliens  all along I granted one piece also has  some moon and space stuff going on but  that's always been well established for  hundreds of chapters instead of suddenly  pulling it out of nowhere at the very  last minutes most anime also deal with a  problem I call power creep the problem  of running into an impossibly strong  villain having the heroes develop a new  power up to defeat them and then rinsing  and repeating over and over until the  powers are just so absurd and don't fit  into the established scope of the  narrative anymore and while one piece  does have cool powers and power-ups it  avoids the problem of power creep that  we see in so many other Series in an  early scene where for example introduced  to one of the literally strongest  characters in the entire series dracul  mihar The Greatest swordsman in the  world one of the seven Warlords of the  sea I mentioned earlier in that  encounter Luffy's crewmate Zorro whose  goal is to become the world's greatest  swordsman himself faces off against him  Zorro who we've seen effortlessly take  out opponents left and right before this  moment is absolutely annihilated by  mihawk and so thanks to this scene and  some others like it we early on get to  see the power ceiling of the world and  that way future power-ups don't just  seem like massive [ __ ] out of  nowhere and instead they seem in line  with the properties of the world as  we've known it right from the start the  consistency of one piece is just  outstanding even the quote-unquote bad  arcs or at least the least favored ones  among the fandoms often surpass the  qualities of many other normal stories  are there occasionally flaws or  inconsistencies  is surprisingly Still Human After All  But the positives of this series  especially giving its massive length  outshine the negatives by far and this  is really mainly thanks to chapter five  the overall tone another reason to watch  One Piece is its tone and this  encapsulate relates a lot of things as  you might guess when Matt Owens a  producer of the upcoming Netflix live  action 1p series was talking about  adapting the series he said one piece  does three things it makes you laugh it  makes you cry and it makes you say holy  sh first and foremost something that  really makes one piece Stand Out Among  its peers is its sense of humor sure  other Shonen often have gags and bits of  humor sprinkled in as well but one piece  really has laughter baked into its core  I mean just look at some of the  character designs but just the  characters itself and the jokes in this  series are just hilarious and the  scenarios that they get themselves into  can be just as funny Luffy having rubber  Powers is essentially just a stretchy  cartoon man sometimes to fight he blows  himself up into a massive balloon once  when fighting a character with  food-based powers he valiantly ate his  way to Victory with the verocious  appetite that only is Shonen  protagonists could have some people do  criticize one piece for its occasional  and Goofy art style which is fair it's  subjective but the truth is that this is  one of its greatest strengths really not  just because it's usually very funny but  also because it makes the emotional and  very serious moments hit just that much  harder like the contrast between you  know just be sitting there just enjoying  your goofy pirate manga when suddenly  you're openly sobbing I don't care if  you have a Heart of Stone you will cry  when you see the suffering that this  cute reindeer has endured for instance  and when you see some of the ridiculous  Stakes that many of these arcs get to  you will be openly stunned when an  entire country of people and characters  you've grown to love are shreddably at  stake and the only possibility of saving  them means Luffy defeating a villain who  has already utterly defeated him  multiple times before that how can you  not be on the edge of your seat and even  if you know deep down that things should  probably work out fine because there are  still hundreds of chapter to go it still  won't stop you from jumping out of Joy  when Loom fee finally beats the big  Baddie lots and lots and lots of reasons  that you need to check out one piece  from the World building to the  characters to the story this is a  must-read experience of media  experiencing the story live along with a  dedicated fan Community isn't something  that you want to miss out on and once  you get caught up you can always come  back to this channel here to enjoy some  of the theories and character analysis  that I've been working on or if you  don't care about being spoiled and you  want to start right now how about  watching the best one piece theory that  you will ever see yes
 

